Below is a step‐by‐step decomposition of the mission description into a hierarchical goal model for a multi‐robot system. In our design, we identify high‐level goals that capture the overall mission (“Deliver Food to Inpatient Room” and “Retrieve Dirty Dishes”) and then decompose these into sub‐goals that address decision making (e.g., selecting the delivery mode based on uncertain inpatient record information) and concrete physical tasks. We use AND and OR (fallback) decompositions as follows:

• An AND decomposition (“;”) is used when all sub‐goals must be performed sequentially or in parallel to satisfy the parent.  
• An OR (fallback) decomposition (“FALLBACK(exp1,exp2)”) is used when fulfilling any one of the alternatives is sufficient to meet the parent’s objective.

We also distinguish between goal types:  
– Perform goals specify activities whose success depends on executing concrete steps.  
– Query goals are used to retrieve uncertain information.  
– Achieve goals specify a desired world state (target condition).

